# S3 — invite mint -> consume (live-e2e Phase 1 scenario 3, M1-546).
#
# The admin mints a single-use OPEN invite (no --contact: the consumer is
# unknown to the bot before it consumes), the code is captured from the
# reply, and the un-registered user consumes it (D44 registration).
# The --open path is confirm-gated (spec §Admin: only --contact skips the
# confirm because its blast radius is one identity) — live-discovered
# 2026-07-03: the first call replies with the confirm prompt, the code is
# minted only on the confirm call.
#
# Host preconditions (HANDOFF §Live-run notes): 'user' must be UNREGISTERED —
# run prod/live-reset.sh first (the admin token re-arms by design D-live-7;
# re-claim before driving). Run s04 before this scenario: s03 registers 'user'.

send dm admin /invite create --adapter simplex --open
expect substring 60000 About to mint an OPEN invite

send dm admin /invite create --open confirm
expect substring 60000 Invite code:
capture code ([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12})

send dm user ${code}
expect substring 60000 Welcome! You're registered.
